<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="h-100">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no" />
    {# The page's own, or the site's if it has none.

       Not truncated here. A search engine cuts a description around 160
       characters, and cutting it in code would mean guessing where -- so each
       one is written to fit instead. The longest of them is 143, on the city
       with the longest name we sell to; if one ever needs more room than that,
       the fix is shorter words rather than an ellipsis. #}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description|default('')|trim ?: config('app.name') ~ ' – ' ~ config('meta.description') }}" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="{{ config('app.name') }}, {{ config('meta.keywords')|join(', ') }}" />
    <meta name="author" content="{{ config('meta.author.name') }} <{{ config('meta.author.email') }}>"/>
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="{{ csrf_token() }}" />

    <title>{{ page_title|default('Flights') }} - {{ config('app.name') }}</title>

    {# The one address this page answers at. A trailing slash is optional here
       and any query string makes another copy, so without this every page
       competes with three or four of itself. #}
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_path() }}" />

    {# Search results are a snapshot of prices that will be wrong tomorrow,
       checkout is a step in a transaction, and /my is one browser's own
       bookings. None of them is a page anybody should arrive at cold. #}
    {% if not indexable() %}
        <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
    {% endif %}

    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>✈️</text></svg>" />

    {# Plus Jakarta Sans is self-hosted -- the @font-face rules are the first
       section of main.css. This preload is the one subset every page renders,
       fetched in parallel with the stylesheet instead of waiting for it to be
       parsed. The other subsets are left to unicode-range.

       `crossorigin` is required even though the file is same-origin: fonts are
       always fetched in CORS mode, and without it the preload is not reused and
       the file downloads twice. The URL must also match what the stylesheet
       asks for exactly -- no cache-buster here, for the same reason. #}
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ config('site.directory.fonts') }}/plus-jakarta-sans-latin.woff2"
          as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />

    <link href="{{ cdn(config('site.static.endpoint.vendor')) }}/mdi-font/css/material-design-iconic-font.min.css" rel="stylesheet" media="all" />
    <link href="//cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/ion-rangeslider/2.3.0/css/ion.rangeSlider.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <link href="//use.fontawesome.com/releases/v6.1.1/css/all.css" rel="stylesheet" type='text/css' integrity="sha384-/frq1SRXYH/bSyou/HUp/hib7RVN1TawQYja658FEOodR/FQBKVqT9Ol+Oz3Olq5" crossorigin="anonymous" />
    <link href="//cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.8/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    {# Only where a map is drawn. See the `map` block in layout.html.twig. #}
    {% if needs_map|default(false) %}
        <link href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/{{ config('maps.gl_version') }}/mapbox-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    {% endif %}
    <link href="{{ asset(config('site.directory.css') ~ '/main.css') }}" rel="stylesheet" media="all" />

    <script src="//code.jquery.com/jquery-3.3.1.min.js"></script>

    {# Nothing loads until somebody has said yes. Both vendors set their own
       cookies and Metrika records the session, so loading them first would make
       the notice at the bottom of the page decoration. See src/Consent.php. #}
    {% if consent.accepted %}
        {% include 'partials/counters.html.twig' %}
    {% endif %}
</head>

{# The active currency, for the two things the browser formats itself: the
   price slider's pill, which converts a Canadian-dollar value as it is dragged,
   and the fare calendar's fallback before a response arrives. On <body> because
   both live on pages that include no partial in common, and because
   document.body.dataset is readable from anywhere in global.js.

   `rate` is here for the slider only. Its values are Canadian dollars and stay
   that way -- they are what the filter compares and what a shared link carries
   -- so only the caption converts. See Helper::sliderCaption. #}
<body class="d-flex flex-column"
      data-currency="{{ currency.active }}"
      data-currency-symbol="{{ currency.symbol }}"
      data-currency-before="{{ currency.before ? '1' : '0' }}"
      data-currency-group="{{ currency.group }}"
      data-currency-rate="{{ currency.rate }}">
<header class="p-3 bg-primary text-white" id="top">
    <div class="container">
        {# Named because the breadcrumb below is a second <nav>, and two
           unlabelled landmarks of the same role are indistinguishable. #}
        <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg bg-primary" data-bs-theme="dark" aria-label="Main">
            <div class="container-fluid">
                <!--a href="/" class="d-flex align-items-center mb-2 mb-lg-0 text-white text-decoration-none me-5"-->
                <a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center mb-2 mb-lg-0 text-decoration-none me-5 text-white" href="/">
                    <i class="fas fa-lg fa-plane-departure pe-3"></i>
                    <strong class="lead">{{ config('app.name') }}</strong>
                </a>
                <button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarSupportedContent" aria-controls="navbarSupportedContent" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Toggle navigation">
                    <span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span>
                </button>
                <div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarSupportedContent">
                    {# Pushed right: the logo owns the left, and the menu is a
                       set of places to go rather than the page's subject. #}
                    {# The section tray.

                       Rendered here on every page but the homepage, which
                       starts it in its hero and has global.js lift it in once
                       the hero has scrolled past -- so this stays empty there
                       until it arrives, and there is never a second copy.

                       Flights is the current section anywhere in the search
                       funnel, which is every page that is not one of the
                       others; Saved marks itself on its own page. #}
                    <div class="navbar-dock js-header-dock">
                        {% if current_page() != '/' %}
                            {% include 'partials/sections.html.twig' with {
                                'docked': true,
                                'current': in_section('/search') or in_section('/checkout'),
                                'saved': in_section('/my/saved/')
                            } only %}
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>

                    <ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto mb-2 mb-lg-0">
                        {% for link, item in config('site.main-menu')|filter(item => item.enabled and (item.header ?? true)) %}
                        <li class="nav-item me-{{ item.spacer|default(2) }}">
                            {# Two different questions. The highlight marks the section you
                               are in, so "My bookings" stays lit on a single booking --
                               exact equality is why it used to go dark there. aria-current
                               stays exact, because an ancestor is not the current page and
                               the breadcrumb's last crumb is already claiming that. #}
                            {% set is_page = current_page() == (link|trim('/', 'right')) %}
                            <a class="nav-link{{ in_section(link) ? ' active' : '' }}"{% if is_page %} aria-current="page"{% endif %} href="{{ link }}">
                                <i class="{{ item.icon }} fa-lg me-2"></i>{{ item.text }}
                            </a>
                        </li>
                        {% endfor %}

                        {# Last in the row, where the placeholder was. A control
                           rather than a link, so it sits outside the loop above
                           -- see the note in site.php on why it left that map. #}
                        <li class="nav-item">
                            {% include 'partials/currency-switcher.html.twig' %}
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    {# There was a "User profile" item here, an avatar and a
                       label with no href, wired to a dialog apologising that it
                       does nothing. There is no account system -- a booking
                       belongs to a session -- and everything personal the app
                       does have, bookings and saved flights, is already in the
                       nav above. An avatar in the account slot of a booking app
                       promises somewhere to sign in. Authorship, which is what
                       the avatar actually showed, is credited in the footer. #}
                </div>
            </div>
        </nav>
    </div>
</header>
